§ `116A. Electronic records`

`s116A(1) a device that ordinarily produces the record` MEANS `Electronic Record Facts` WITH
    `the kind of proceedings` IS `criminal proceedings`
    `the device or process is one that, or is of a kind that, if properly used, ordinarily produces or accurately communicates an electronic record` IS TRUE
    `evidence sufficient to raise doubt about the presumption is adduced` IS FALSE
    `the electronic record was generated, recorded or stored in the usual and ordinary course of business by a person who was not a party to the proceedings on the occasion in question` IS FALSE
    `that person did not generate, record or store it under the control of the party seeking to introduce it` IS FALSE
    `the electronic record was generated, recorded or stored by a party adverse in interest to the party seeking to adduce it` IS FALSE
    `the person who generated, recorded or stored it was a police officer or other officer of a law enforcement agency involved in the investigation of the offences allegedly committed by the accused person` IS FALSE
    `the person who generated, recorded or stored it was an accomplice of the accused person, whether or not charged in the same proceedings` IS FALSE
    `evidence to the contrary is adduced` IS FALSE
    `the electronic record was recorded or stored from a document produced pursuant to an approved process` IS FALSE

