§ `103 to 113. Burden of proof`

`s104 ill a the claimant to land` MEANS `Burden Facts` WITH
    `the party who would fail if no evidence at all were given on either side is the party who asserts the fact` IS TRUE
    `a law provides that the proof of the fact is to lie on a particular person` IS FALSE
    `the fact is necessary to be proved in order to enable a person to give evidence of another fact` IS FALSE
    `the person is accused of an offence` IS FALSE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a general exception in the Penal Code 1871` IS FALSE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a special exception or proviso contained in another part of the Penal Code 1871` IS FALSE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a special exception or proviso contained in a law defining the offence` IS FALSE
    `the fact is especially within the knowledge of a person` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is alive or dead and it is shown that the person was alive within 30 years` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is alive or dead and it is proved that the person has not been heard of for 7 years by those who would naturally have heard of the person if alive` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether persons are partners, landlord and tenant, or principal and agent, and it has been shown that they have been acting as such` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is the owner of a thing of which the person is shown to be in possession` IS FALSE
    `there is a question as to the good faith of a transaction between parties one of whom stands to the other in a position of active confidence` IS FALSE

`s104 ill b the defendant who alleges fraud` MEANS `Burden Facts` WITH
    `the party who would fail if no evidence at all were given on either side is the party who asserts the fact` IS FALSE
